1
00:00:02,730 --> 00:00:06,150
<i>Man, today was crazy.</i>

2
00:00:06,810 --> 00:00:10,600
<i>Feels like I lived a full week in one day.</i>

3
00:00:17,830 --> 00:00:19,370
<i>What? Why? How?</i>

4
00:00:19,590 --> 00:00:23,000
<i>What possessed Himari to do that?!</i>

5
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:24,260
<i>It was so out of left field,</i>

6
00:00:24,260 --> 00:00:26,590
<i>my emotions can hardly keep up!</i>

7
00:00:28,660 --> 00:00:31,250
Times like these call for flowers.

8
00:00:32,720 --> 00:00:36,250
You think Himari kissed me 
cause she likes me like <i>that</i>?

9
00:00:36,800 --> 00:00:39,470
How the hell am I supposed to 
act around Hima—

10
00:00:39,470 --> 00:00:40,720
Hey Natsu.

11
00:00:41,410 --> 00:00:44,720
Having fun talking 
to flowers all by yourself?

12
00:01:06,500 --> 00:01:08,960
Can a Boy-Girl Friendship Survive?

13
00:01:07,370 --> 00:01:08,960
(No, It Can't!!)

14
00:02:16,570 --> 00:02:19,690
I know you're plotting 
behind my back with Kureha-san.

15
00:02:16,570 --> 00:02:20,990
Goodbye, Sunflower

16
00:02:19,870 --> 00:02:22,290
Huh? Nope, I don't know anything about that.

17
00:02:22,660 --> 00:02:24,790
I'm not involved this time.

18
00:02:25,160 --> 00:02:26,210
You're not?

19
00:02:26,360 --> 00:02:27,440
Well, I tried.

20
00:02:27,440 --> 00:02:29,710
But she used me for info 
and tossed me aside.

21
00:02:30,240 --> 00:02:33,880
I guess she prefers to work alone.

22
00:02:34,240 --> 00:02:37,840
Then why didn't you 
convince her to let Hima—

23
00:02:37,840 --> 00:02:38,880
I can't do that!

24
00:02:41,570 --> 00:02:46,280
You still want Himari to go to Tokyo, huh?

25
00:02:46,800 --> 00:02:48,190
Not exactly.

26
00:02:48,670 --> 00:02:49,120
Huh?

27
00:02:49,540 --> 00:02:52,070
I'd never turn my back on Kureha-san.

28
00:02:52,850 --> 00:02:53,980
Because I love her.

29
00:02:55,400 --> 00:02:57,090
Got a problem with that?

30
00:02:57,090 --> 00:02:59,450
I can fall in love too, you know!

31
00:02:59,680 --> 00:03:01,070
N-Never mind that!

32
00:03:01,070 --> 00:03:02,090
What about you?

33
00:03:03,200 --> 00:03:04,650
N-Nothing much.

34
00:03:04,650 --> 00:03:05,760
Come on!

35
00:03:05,760 --> 00:03:08,940
After everything I just told you?

36
00:03:08,940 --> 00:03:11,520
What's this about smooching Himari-chan?

37
00:03:12,500 --> 00:03:15,400
I-I-I don't remember telling you that!

38
00:03:15,820 --> 00:03:17,940
Technically, you didn't.

39
00:03:17,940 --> 00:03:20,770
I'd be more careful talking to flowers.

40
00:03:20,770 --> 00:03:22,490
So? Did you confess?

41
00:03:23,130 --> 00:03:26,230
No... We went to the Sunflower Festival.

42
00:03:26,460 --> 00:03:30,260
She kept mentioning Enomoto-san, 
when she suddenly...

43
00:03:30,950 --> 00:03:32,270
So that's how.

44
00:03:33,530 --> 00:03:34,720
This is perfect!

45
00:03:34,720 --> 00:03:39,890
I figured I had no role to play this time, 
but this changes everything!

46
00:03:40,500 --> 00:03:42,900
You seem to be having lots of fun.

47
00:03:43,090 --> 00:03:48,400
Either way, I doubt you 
can act like friends now.

48
00:03:48,580 --> 00:03:50,420
I-I guess not.

49
00:03:51,110 --> 00:03:55,670
Then I suggest you focus 
on the task at hand.

50
00:03:58,550 --> 00:03:59,430
See ya.

51
00:04:01,640 --> 00:04:03,230
<i>Makishima's right.</i>

52
00:04:03,800 --> 00:04:06,160
<i>If I lose this battle, 
I'd have to give up Himari.</i>

53
00:04:06,740 --> 00:04:08,630
<i>There's only one thing I can do now.</i>

54
00:04:09,310 --> 00:04:12,390
<i>Focus on making my masterpiece, like always!</i>

55
00:04:14,760 --> 00:04:17,820
<i>Look at all these delicious 
dumplings I made for everyone.</i>

56
00:04:18,230 --> 00:04:23,040
<i>Lemme dive in first on this 
springy sandwich of goodness.</i>

57
00:04:23,220 --> 00:04:24,320
<i>Here I go!</i>

58
00:04:24,960 --> 00:04:26,500
<i>Yum, yum.</i>

59
00:04:27,080 --> 00:04:30,650
<i>Yum, yum, yum.</i>

60
00:04:31,030 --> 00:04:35,060
<i>Yummy, yummy.</i>

61
00:04:35,070 --> 00:04:40,320
<i>Yummy, yummy, yum, yum, yum...</i>

62
00:04:58,300 --> 00:04:59,240
<i>Did that happen?</i>

63
00:04:59,520 --> 00:05:01,490
<i>What have I done?</i>

64
00:05:01,690 --> 00:05:02,810
<i>Oh my gosh!</i>

65
00:05:02,810 --> 00:05:03,760
It's not a dream?

66
00:05:03,760 --> 00:05:04,760
Please, let it be a dream!

67
00:05:04,760 --> 00:05:07,480
Why did I do that?!

68
00:05:08,730 --> 00:05:10,500
How can I even message him?

69
00:05:10,500 --> 00:05:12,640
What do I even say?

70
00:05:13,180 --> 00:05:15,400
<i>"Which is more springy?"</i>

71
00:05:15,400 --> 00:05:16,920
<i>"Dumplings or my lips?"</i>

72
00:05:16,920 --> 00:05:18,600
Shut up, you idiot!

73
00:05:18,600 --> 00:05:23,280
What kind of high school girl says that?!

74
00:05:23,770 --> 00:05:25,180
<i>He hates me. I know it.</i>

75
00:05:25,180 --> 00:05:26,590
Himari? Can I come in?

76
00:05:27,560 --> 00:05:28,440
<i>It's Onii-chan!</i>

77
00:05:28,440 --> 00:05:30,200
<i>I can't let him find out!</i>

78
00:05:31,990 --> 00:05:34,000
Going somewhere?

79
00:05:36,520 --> 00:05:37,460
I see.

80
00:05:37,840 --> 00:05:40,890
You were annoyed by his 
wishy-washy attitude,

81
00:05:40,890 --> 00:05:43,440
so you kissed him on impulse.

82
00:05:45,620 --> 00:05:47,780
Oh well. What's done is done.

83
00:05:50,240 --> 00:05:52,490
You thought I would scold you?

84
00:05:53,000 --> 00:05:57,620
You deserve praise 
for being true to your feelings.

85
00:05:58,050 --> 00:06:02,140
Besides, if you get dumped, 
I can swoop in to save the day!

86
00:06:02,790 --> 00:06:04,840
So no worries!

87
00:06:05,040 --> 00:06:08,210
<i>I totally forgot. He lives for this stuff.</i>

88
00:06:08,560 --> 00:06:11,410
Well, time for me to eat dinner.

89
00:06:13,520 --> 00:06:16,350
I noticed the smell of delicious dumplings.

90
00:06:16,580 --> 00:06:19,640
R-Right, Onii-chan...

91
00:06:19,880 --> 00:06:22,880
About the dumplings...

92
00:06:24,270 --> 00:06:25,780
The hell is this?!

93
00:06:25,780 --> 00:06:28,290
There isn't a single one left!

94
00:06:29,000 --> 00:06:31,990
I'm sorry!

95
00:06:31,990 --> 00:06:34,450
Science Room

96
00:06:32,960 --> 00:06:33,890
<i>I can't tell.</i>

97
00:06:34,450 --> 00:06:38,870
<i>They might be done. They might not.</i>

98
00:06:39,340 --> 00:06:41,360
<i>Ever since yesterday, 
I keep thinking of Himari.</i>

99
00:06:41,360 --> 00:06:43,190
<i>I can't focus.</i>

100
00:06:44,110 --> 00:06:45,780
Yu-kun, what's up?

101
00:06:46,860 --> 00:06:48,400
Enomoto-san! Don't you have practice?

102
00:06:48,640 --> 00:06:50,890
I decided to come by for lunch.

103
00:06:51,040 --> 00:06:53,340
It's lunch time already?

104
00:06:54,570 --> 00:06:56,850
Were you about to take these out?

105
00:06:57,150 --> 00:06:58,500
I'm not sure yet.

106
00:06:58,870 --> 00:07:00,220
Even if it looks done on the surface,

107
00:07:00,220 --> 00:07:02,810
it might still have 
coloring left in the center.

108
00:07:03,330 --> 00:07:04,480
If it's not done all the way,

109
00:07:04,480 --> 00:07:06,160
it could cause problems later on.

110
00:07:06,720 --> 00:07:09,920
Oh, are these the ones 
you got with Hii-chan?

111
00:07:09,920 --> 00:07:10,880
Y-Yup.

112
00:07:11,150 --> 00:07:13,830
You picked them out while you kissed?

113
00:07:14,170 --> 00:07:18,990
Actually, we picked them out 
and then we kiss—

114
00:07:22,510 --> 00:07:24,750
Makishima told you, huh?

115
00:07:25,000 --> 00:07:28,460
Yup. Darn. I wish I went.

116
00:07:29,110 --> 00:07:31,420
I wouldn't have let Hii-chan get ahead.

117
00:07:31,640 --> 00:07:34,380
I'm not sure how to respond to that.

118
00:07:35,340 --> 00:07:36,670
Listen, Enomoto-san.

119
00:07:37,720 --> 00:07:41,200
I think I need to tell Himari how I feel.

120
00:07:42,340 --> 00:07:43,170
Good for you.

121
00:07:43,900 --> 00:07:44,400
You think so?

122
00:07:45,080 --> 00:07:48,580
To me, it makes no difference 
whether you two go out.

123
00:07:49,110 --> 00:07:50,800
Even if you were dating from the start,

124
00:07:50,800 --> 00:07:52,320
I would have told you how I felt.

125
00:07:52,600 --> 00:07:55,770
<i>Oh yeah, that's how she is.</i>

126
00:07:56,080 --> 00:07:59,240
I'm gonna be Hii-chan's number one friend.

127
00:07:59,530 --> 00:08:03,760
Maybe one day, she'll agree 
to share you with me.

128
00:08:04,480 --> 00:08:05,820
That's my end goal!

129
00:08:06,250 --> 00:08:07,720
I'll get back to practice.

130
00:08:10,190 --> 00:08:10,670
See ya later.

131
00:08:19,140 --> 00:08:22,640
H-Hey, um... I...

132
00:08:23,030 --> 00:08:24,020
Punishment!

133
00:08:29,880 --> 00:08:31,380
Himari! You okay?!

134
00:08:31,380 --> 00:08:32,640
She was for real that time!

135
00:08:32,640 --> 00:08:36,160
I was about to die!

136
00:08:41,590 --> 00:08:43,780
L-Look, Himari.

137
00:08:44,620 --> 00:08:47,670
I'm not gonna pretend like 
yesterday didn't happen.

138
00:08:49,430 --> 00:08:50,950
So... um...

139
00:08:52,420 --> 00:08:55,270
There's something I need to tell you 
after I beat Kureha-san!

140
00:08:55,600 --> 00:08:56,050
Sure.

141
00:08:56,470 --> 00:08:58,230
<i>Okay, now what?</i>

142
00:08:58,590 --> 00:09:01,210
<i>I didn't think about how to act 
after saying that!</i>

143
00:09:01,480 --> 00:09:02,660
<i>I need a diversion!</i>

144
00:09:04,450 --> 00:09:06,440
<i>I think it's about the right time...</i>

145
00:09:07,000 --> 00:09:09,080
<i>Oh well, here goes nothing!</i>

146
00:09:12,840 --> 00:09:15,110
What do you plan to make with these?

147
00:09:15,890 --> 00:09:17,360
A sunflower tiara.

148
00:09:18,610 --> 00:09:19,570
That sounds amazing!

149
00:09:22,370 --> 00:09:28,640
<i>Her smile was even cuter than that time... 
before my middle school exhibit.</i>

150
00:09:31,240 --> 00:09:33,510
You're gonna be gone for the Obon holidays?

151
00:09:33,510 --> 00:09:34,240
Yup.

152
00:09:34,530 --> 00:09:39,480
We're going on a family trip 
while my dad's back home.

153
00:09:39,840 --> 00:09:41,960
Oh... How about you, Enomoto-san?

154
00:09:42,320 --> 00:09:43,480
I have to help out at the store.

155
00:09:43,980 --> 00:09:46,220
Our cakes sell out during Obon.

156
00:09:46,440 --> 00:09:48,270
It's the busy season, then.

157
00:09:49,240 --> 00:09:52,950
I can't work at home 
with my older sisters visiting.

158
00:09:53,320 --> 00:09:55,320
But school's closed during break.

159
00:09:55,320 --> 00:09:57,200
I gotta figure out a workspace.

160
00:09:57,200 --> 00:09:59,170
Why don't you use our place then?

161
00:09:59,170 --> 00:10:00,440
I'll let Onii-chan know.

162
00:10:00,770 --> 00:10:03,140
For real? Thanks!

163
00:10:47,060 --> 00:10:49,190
<i>Three more days until the match.</i>

164
00:10:50,860 --> 00:10:52,290
Wow, Yu-kun.

165
00:10:52,520 --> 00:10:54,540
You worked so hard.

166
00:10:55,080 --> 00:10:56,560
Your tiara's great.

167
00:10:59,330 --> 00:11:01,670
Kureha-kun won't stand a chance.

168
00:11:02,320 --> 00:11:03,720
Thank you.

169
00:11:03,920 --> 00:11:06,800
Finally, you'll get to 
be my little brother for real.

170
00:11:06,800 --> 00:11:10,880
Let's say cheers 
with the tiara to celebrate!

171
00:11:11,400 --> 00:11:13,310
I showed you yesterday too, though.

172
00:11:14,950 --> 00:11:17,380
It's so good, I can't get enough!

173
00:11:23,640 --> 00:11:25,990
Yu-kun, what happened?

174
00:11:26,640 --> 00:11:27,440
<i>What's going on?</i>

175
00:11:28,060 --> 00:11:29,630
<i>How did this happen?</i>

176
00:11:30,280 --> 00:11:33,580
<i>The flowers are dying 
from losing their inner moisture.</i>

177
00:11:36,000 --> 00:11:39,190
<i>Did I mess up the timing back then?</i>

178
00:11:41,670 --> 00:11:44,050
Can this be fixed somehow?

179
00:11:45,690 --> 00:11:48,050
No, not at this point.

180
00:11:48,550 --> 00:11:51,010
I can tidy up how it looks 
but not the quality.

181
00:11:51,380 --> 00:11:52,070
Any spares?

182
00:11:52,780 --> 00:11:55,020
I was so focused on making just one.

183
00:11:55,020 --> 00:11:57,110
I used them all up in trial runs.

184
00:11:59,280 --> 00:12:01,940
Yu-kun, I'll grab the car.

185
00:12:01,940 --> 00:12:03,830
Let's go look for sunflowers.

186
00:12:04,320 --> 00:12:06,750
We'll search stores across the city—

187
00:12:05,940 --> 00:12:06,750
Hibari-san.

188
00:12:07,810 --> 00:12:09,490
You've been drinking.

189
00:12:23,390 --> 00:12:24,300
There.

190
00:12:29,600 --> 00:12:31,070
Yu-kun, I'm coming in.

191
00:12:32,410 --> 00:12:33,660
Good morning.

192
00:12:37,890 --> 00:12:39,300
Morning...

193
00:12:41,590 --> 00:12:46,840
It's been a while since I had some
 quality Yu time. Put me right to sleep.

194
00:12:46,970 --> 00:12:49,460
I needed that to rejuvenate 
myself after my trip.

195
00:12:49,840 --> 00:12:51,830
You say that like I'm a beauty treatment.

196
00:12:52,080 --> 00:12:55,230
Seems like trouble broke out 
while I was gone.

197
00:12:55,640 --> 00:12:56,560
Sorry.

198
00:12:56,720 --> 00:12:59,470
Let's see the final product!

199
00:12:59,640 --> 00:13:00,670
Right!

200
00:13:01,410 --> 00:13:05,060
Wow! It's so cute!

201
00:13:05,060 --> 00:13:06,150
Don't you think Onii-chan?

202
00:13:07,460 --> 00:13:09,270
I think it's a good piece.

203
00:13:10,380 --> 00:13:13,680
I'm proud of you for bouncing back 
in a matter of a few days.

204
00:13:17,860 --> 00:13:20,320
Can I go ahead and take a look?

205
00:13:20,490 --> 00:13:21,060
Please.

206
00:13:25,800 --> 00:13:28,550
Wow, it's so cute!

207
00:13:28,550 --> 00:13:31,780
It looks much better 
than the ones on social media.

208
00:13:33,040 --> 00:13:35,600
Is this a wedding tiara?

209
00:13:35,600 --> 00:13:38,680
The sunflowers are so bold. 
What a fashion statement.

210
00:13:38,900 --> 00:13:42,970
I like the attention to detail, too.

211
00:13:43,390 --> 00:13:45,760
You really think so?

212
00:13:46,240 --> 00:13:49,470
Yup! It's definitely cute.

213
00:13:49,470 --> 00:13:51,380
I actually want it for myself.

214
00:13:52,390 --> 00:13:54,840
You mean I won the matc—

215
00:13:54,110 --> 00:13:56,580
Hmm, I dunno about that.

216
00:13:56,580 --> 00:13:59,110
It's cute, but not good enough!

217
00:13:59,510 --> 00:14:01,740
But you just said you want it!

218
00:14:02,820 --> 00:14:07,040
Were you planning on saying that either way?

219
00:14:08,470 --> 00:14:11,110
I'd never do something that unfair.

220
00:14:11,110 --> 00:14:13,360
If you actually made something good,

221
00:14:13,360 --> 00:14:16,620
I was planning on giving up Himari-chan.

222
00:14:16,900 --> 00:14:18,310
Then why?

223
00:14:18,830 --> 00:14:20,260
It's obvious, isn't it?

224
00:14:20,260 --> 00:14:24,530
You were supposed to give 
it your all in this match.

225
00:14:24,840 --> 00:14:28,670
But you tried to play it off 
with a failed piece.

226
00:14:28,670 --> 00:14:31,890
And <i>I'm</i> being unfair?

227
00:14:33,230 --> 00:14:34,860
That's not true.

228
00:14:35,190 --> 00:14:37,020
I always put my all into every piec—

229
00:14:37,020 --> 00:14:40,180
Then why did you bring me a back-up piece?

230
00:14:43,160 --> 00:14:45,590
I heard about the flowers dying.

231
00:14:45,590 --> 00:14:48,770
Sakura-chan told me so.

232
00:14:50,000 --> 00:14:52,440
You tried to trick me.

233
00:14:52,930 --> 00:14:55,740
Why didn't you tell me the truth?

234
00:14:55,740 --> 00:14:58,580
But if I could just make it in time—

235
00:14:58,580 --> 00:15:01,040
If you did, then what?

236
00:15:05,450 --> 00:15:07,740
You said he was your best creator.

237
00:15:07,940 --> 00:15:09,940
What a waste of time.

238
00:15:11,340 --> 00:15:13,440
All right, Rion! Let's go home.

239
00:15:13,850 --> 00:15:16,840
I should say hi to mom for a change.

240
00:15:26,200 --> 00:15:27,990
You have something to say?

241
00:15:28,500 --> 00:15:31,870
Why did you tell Kureha-san 
about the flowers dying?

242
00:15:32,060 --> 00:15:35,490
What were you about 
to tell Kureha back there?

243
00:15:39,240 --> 00:15:40,100
Let me guess.

244
00:15:40,390 --> 00:15:44,000
"If I could just make it 
in time, it'd be fine."

245
00:15:44,590 --> 00:15:49,420
If you're not serious about 
accessories, give it up already.

246
00:15:49,730 --> 00:15:53,520
Saku-nee-san, you're saying 
I'm not serious about it?

247
00:15:55,800 --> 00:15:57,800
You remember these?

248
00:16:02,840 --> 00:16:04,020
The returned pieces...

249
00:16:05,320 --> 00:16:10,330
When I spoke with Sasaki-sensei, 
he was very understanding.

250
00:16:10,610 --> 00:16:13,990
Other than one thing: 
the quality of the pieces.

251
00:16:14,390 --> 00:16:15,340
What do you mean?

252
00:16:16,610 --> 00:16:17,660
Take a closer look.

253
00:16:21,420 --> 00:16:23,630
There's two more with the same issue.

254
00:16:24,080 --> 00:16:26,280
And another one with a cracked petal.

255
00:16:26,880 --> 00:16:29,320
You understand what this means?

256
00:16:31,060 --> 00:16:36,160
Remember when I said your pieces 
were frozen in time?

257
00:16:36,640 --> 00:16:37,210
Yeah...

258
00:16:37,760 --> 00:16:42,750
Until then, you'd never sold 
a defective product.

259
00:16:43,370 --> 00:16:47,200
But after I told you that, 
you've made four bad pieces.

260
00:16:49,040 --> 00:16:51,520
Your past work showed 
that you gave it your all.

261
00:16:51,930 --> 00:16:57,200
But all it took was a little play on 
romance to get you off your game.

262
00:16:58,520 --> 00:17:01,580
You're not cut out to be a creator.

263
00:17:02,160 --> 00:17:06,440
You couldn't even get serious 
for this match with your dream at stake.

264
00:17:07,090 --> 00:17:10,820
Get your head straight 
if you really want to be a creator.

265
00:17:11,360 --> 00:17:15,620
Keep customers out of it 
if you're going to prioritize romance.

266
00:17:16,240 --> 00:17:20,980
Feel ashamed for toying around 
with this ridiculous tiara in a dire match.

267
00:17:25,760 --> 00:17:27,150
Hey, Yu...

268
00:17:27,600 --> 00:17:28,430
Himari.

269
00:17:29,080 --> 00:17:31,320
About what I said before I made this tiara.

270
00:17:32,080 --> 00:17:33,730
Sorry. Forget I said anything.

271
00:17:35,600 --> 00:17:36,140
Himari.

272
00:17:37,590 --> 00:17:38,160
Let's go.

273
00:17:47,780 --> 00:17:49,840
What did you bring me out here for?

274
00:17:50,530 --> 00:17:54,660
Sorry, but I don't plan 
on going to Tokyo like you want.

275
00:17:55,600 --> 00:17:57,560
You heard from Natsu, right?

276
00:17:57,860 --> 00:17:59,990
I'm not involved in this one.

277
00:18:00,630 --> 00:18:03,320
My plans start from here.

278
00:18:04,660 --> 00:18:05,490
Himari-chan.

279
00:18:05,970 --> 00:18:10,030
Join Kureha-san's agency 
and aim for the top.

280
00:18:10,250 --> 00:18:14,680
Excuse me? I told you 
my promise with Yu comes first.

281
00:18:15,160 --> 00:18:19,020
I know that's not easy to say, 
especially with finances.

282
00:18:20,130 --> 00:18:24,450
Isn't that more of a reason 
to accept Kureha-san's offer?

283
00:18:24,850 --> 00:18:25,910
What do you mean?

284
00:18:26,930 --> 00:18:30,520
It's the perfect opportunity 
to get your name out there.

285
00:18:30,960 --> 00:18:33,490
All the more if you want to 
promote Natsu's accessories.

286
00:18:34,670 --> 00:18:37,160
Your strength is your charm.

287
00:18:37,720 --> 00:18:40,640
Go learn how to best 
leverage those strengths.

288
00:18:41,060 --> 00:18:43,440
Accepting Kureha-san's offer 
is only your ticket.

289
00:18:43,810 --> 00:18:46,570
B-But I have to support Yu.

290
00:18:46,570 --> 00:18:48,210
Rin-chan can do that.

291
00:18:48,530 --> 00:18:49,440
Still!

292
00:18:51,240 --> 00:18:54,110
I'm not telling you to hand him over.

293
00:18:54,490 --> 00:18:56,520
Just to let her borrow him.

294
00:18:57,120 --> 00:19:01,950
If your bond's the real deal, 
a few years apart can't hurt.

295
00:19:02,460 --> 00:19:04,760
<i>The real deal?</i>

296
00:19:08,110 --> 00:19:09,480
How about this?

297
00:19:10,130 --> 00:19:12,720
One day, when you two's dream comes true,

298
00:19:12,720 --> 00:19:15,590
and you still feel 
the same way towards Natsu,

299
00:19:15,970 --> 00:19:20,140
I promise to help you 
with everything I've got.

300
00:19:21,480 --> 00:19:23,410
I might be a player, 
but I can keep a promise.

301
00:19:24,440 --> 00:19:26,560
Think about it.

302
00:19:28,090 --> 00:19:32,070
<i>It's my fault for drowning in romance 
and throwing aside friendship.</i>

303
00:19:32,720 --> 00:19:35,270
<i>All while Yu was serious about his work.</i>

304
00:19:37,540 --> 00:19:40,520
<i>I was the one who screwed everything up.</i>

305
00:19:45,690 --> 00:19:49,400
Is this the last time 
I get to cling onto you?

306
00:19:49,400 --> 00:19:52,240
Kinda makes you think, doesn't it?

307
00:19:53,390 --> 00:19:56,770
It's hot enough as it is. Get off.

308
00:19:57,100 --> 00:20:00,420
Don't cheat on me while I'm gone, okay?

309
00:20:00,420 --> 00:20:04,680
Who's cheating? We're not even dating.

310
00:20:05,130 --> 00:20:09,110
Don't say that like you're 
not crazy for me.

311
00:20:09,110 --> 00:20:13,110
You didn't even accept 
an offer from Enocchi.

312
00:20:15,000 --> 00:20:15,920
By the way, Himari.

313
00:20:17,240 --> 00:20:18,810
You're not gonna "Bwa-ha!" at me today?

314
00:20:21,200 --> 00:20:26,590
Feels like one of those 
crossroads in life, doesn't it?

315
00:20:27,920 --> 00:20:30,440
If I become a famous model,

316
00:20:30,440 --> 00:20:33,000
I can promote your accessories even more.

317
00:20:33,240 --> 00:20:35,910
Which means our dream will come true.

318
00:20:36,560 --> 00:20:37,680
Maybe, yeah.

319
00:20:38,000 --> 00:20:42,860
Or I could beg my grandpa 
to pay off my debt.

320
00:20:42,860 --> 00:20:47,990
Which means we could live out our cute, 
raunchy high school dreams!

321
00:20:47,990 --> 00:20:49,100
Don't say it like that!

322
00:20:49,300 --> 00:20:51,080
That's an awful way to put it.

323
00:20:54,590 --> 00:20:56,790
Our future dream or our romance today.

324
00:20:56,790 --> 00:21:00,360
Which one are we supposed to live for?

325
00:21:00,920 --> 00:21:02,670
Himari, don't forget.

326
00:21:03,560 --> 00:21:06,680
If you want me to give up my dream—

327
00:21:08,030 --> 00:21:12,030
J-Jeez, Yu. You're so obsessed with flowers.

328
00:21:12,030 --> 00:21:13,210
No, I'm willing to—

329
00:21:13,210 --> 00:21:16,340
It's all you care about, I get it.

330
00:21:16,340 --> 00:21:17,070
Himari!

331
00:21:17,540 --> 00:21:18,720
Please.

332
00:21:18,960 --> 00:21:22,740
I can't bear you quitting.

333
00:21:24,590 --> 00:21:25,240
I can't.

334
00:21:28,740 --> 00:21:30,450
<i>This world is full of contradictions.</i>

335
00:21:31,210 --> 00:21:36,170
<i>Betting on our future together 
is probably the right thing to do.</i>

336
00:21:36,940 --> 00:21:40,690
<i>But for that, we have no 
choice but to be apart.</i>

337
00:21:40,690 --> 00:21:42,630
<i>It's messed up, but I'll accept it.</i>

338
00:21:44,290 --> 00:21:47,440
<i>Somewhere down this path, 
we'll meet again one day.</i>

339
00:21:48,420 --> 00:21:52,000
<i>Even if our love looks different by then,</i>

340
00:21:52,450 --> 00:21:53,990
<i>I believe we'll still laugh together.</i>

341
00:21:54,460 --> 00:21:56,360
<i>As best friends.</i>

342
00:21:58,430 --> 00:22:01,230
<i>Farewell to our romance.</i>

343
00:22:02,930 --> 00:22:04,160
<i>I wish you well.</i>

344
00:23:35,300 --> 00:23:40,020
Flowers that Bloom Along
 the Path of Dreams

